invariant: INV-27
file: quic_retry.h
catches: test/lint-quic-partition.sh
reason: quic_retry.h moves its #include lines above the transport
  guard, which is ordinary C layout and puts stddef.h's and stdint.h's
  declarations into every TLS build that reads the header. The file
  itself still declares nothing without the define, so the comparison
  of the two runs passes it. The lint also reads the whole translation
  unit of a quic* file, sees the declarations the includes pulled in,
  and names the include as the cause.

--- old
#define CH_QUIC_RETRY_H
#ifdef CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC

#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>
--- new
#define CH_QUIC_RETRY_H

#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>

#ifdef CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC
